From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Agent <claude-agent@invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:59:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] debian: Add nativehdr5 changelog entry

Summarise the color-management input batch: signed custom primaries with
shared fallible matrix validation, ICC range and descriptor fixes, EDID
primaries validation for native SDR, exact encoding and fallback target
serialization, and the creator-params error code fix.
---
 debian/changelog | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/debian/changelog b/debian/changelog
index 16dd137..1035f1c 100644
--- a/debian/changelog
+++ b/debian/changelog
@@ -1,3 +1,24 @@
+mutter (51.0-1ubuntu3+nativehdr5) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium
+
+  * Accept signed custom primaries for encoding gamuts within [-16, 16]
+    without clamping, and decide support with one fallible definition of the
+    renderer's linear BT.2020 matrices shared by the color transform and the
+    Wayland creator: collinear or nearly singular primaries and white points
+    with y <= 0 or outside the primaries fail with 'unsupported'.
+  * Fix ICC file handling: descriptor 0 counts as set, the offset + length
+    range is checked without 32-bit wraparound, descriptors are owned on
+    every rejection path, the profile is read at the absolute offset and a
+    short read fails as 'operating_system', and unusable profile data fails
+    as 'unsupported'.
+  * Validate EDID default primaries before using them for the native SDR
+    output color state; fall back to sRGB colorimetry and warn once.
+  * Publish encoding primaries and the encoding-fallback target primaries
+    with one exact signed round-and-check conversion.
+  * Post the creator-params interface's own unsupported_feature error.
+    Source candidate only; runtime and package qualification pending.
+
+ -- Claude Agent <claude-agent@invalid>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
+
 mutter (51.0-1ubuntu3+nativehdr4) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium
 
   * Publish independent firmware-declared target RGBW on the validated native
